 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-19", "priority": "P3", "status": "pending", "title": "[dogfood:P3] MusterFlow table output truncates wide fields to ~120 chars — discover answers and queue entries unreadable without --output json (musterflow-side, DF-038 filed there)", "detail": "Through the generated CLI (`musterflow Off-by-One discovery discover-solution ...`), the default table renders `answer` as a ~120-char truncated JSON string; the full solution is only visible with `--output json` or `-r/--raw`, and nothing in the truncated output hints at those flags. A real consumer discovers this by trial. Filed as DF-038 on the musterflow board (this repo is the affected consumer); reproduced 2026-09-24 against the live lab. Fix belongs to musterflow (ellipsize with a hint, or wrap), mirrored here only as a consumer note.", "source": "dogfood tick off-by-one-dogfood-2026-09-24-15-47-25", "created_by": "off-by-one-dogfood", "created_at": "2026-09-24", "acceptance_criteria": "musterflow default table either wraps long fields or prints a one-line hint naming --output json; off-by-one docs note the flag for consumers.", "evidence": "CLI transcripts in docs/dogfood/2026-09-24-integration.md (truncated 'answer {...' lines); musterflow board DF-038"}
