-{"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-22", "title": "[dogfood:P1] Export/import round-trip silently DESTROYS community edits — producer re-export overwrites an externally updated answer with no diff/merge, and consumer import can never see the update (silent data loss, no conflict signal)", "priority": "P1", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "labels": ["dogfood", "export-import"], "notes": "Repro 2026-09-25 (scratch producer :18801 / consumer :18802, bare community remote /tmp on local host). 1) Producer exports answers 2,3,4 via POST /api/v1/export -> commit a950ae0, spec 8.1 layout OK. 2) A community editor clones, appends '**Update v2:** ...' to the solution body of go-string-reverse, pushes commit 6720124. 3) Consumer import (conflict_strategy replace) reports {added:0,updated:0,skipped:3} — the update is INVISIBLE (root cause = DF-OFF-BY-ONE-23 parse cut). 4) Producer re-exports answer 4 -> commit 719cec8, and 'grep -c Update v2' in the community repo goes 1 -> 0: the community edit is clobbered with zero warnings — the handler forces Push:true (handlers.go:940) and the engine only skips answers whose own freshly-formatted bytes are identical (writeItem has no upstream-diff check). The edit is now unrecoverable: it never entered any DB (producer import would also report skipped — its stored answer still equals the parsed-cut text). Promised behavior per README component map: 'Pull community answers with diff + conflict resolution'. Fix direction: export engine should refuse or rebase when the working tree contains un-pushed/foreign commits touching the subtree (it already clones, so rev-list origin/main..HEAD tells it); import should land updates when content genuinely differs (currently unreachable for appended-below-marker edits, see DF-23); at minimum surface per-answer detail (handler drops result.Details) so a skipped answer is distinguishable from a destroyed one."}
+{"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-22", "title": "[dogfood:P1] Export/import round-trip silently DESTROYS community edits — producer re-export overwrites an externally updated answer with no diff/merge, and consumer import can never see the update (silent data loss, no conflict signal)", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "labels": ["dogfood", "export-import"], "notes": "Repro 2026-09-25 (scratch producer :18801 / consumer :18802, bare community remote /tmp on local host). 1) Producer exports answers 2,3,4 via POST /api/v1/export -> commit a950ae0, spec 8.1 layout OK. 2) A community editor clones, appends '**Update v2:** ...' to the solution body of go-string-reverse, pushes commit 6720124. 3) Consumer import (conflict_strategy replace) reports {added:0,updated:0,skipped:3} — the update is INVISIBLE (root cause = DF-OFF-BY-ONE-23 parse cut). 4) Producer re-exports answer 4 -> commit 719cec8, and 'grep -c Update v2' in the community repo goes 1 -> 0: the community edit is clobbered with zero warnings — the handler forces Push:true (handlers.go:940) and the engine only skips answers whose own freshly-formatted bytes are identical (writeItem has no upstream-diff check). The edit is now unrecoverable: it never entered any DB (producer import would also report skipped — its stored answer still equals the parsed-cut text). Promised behavior per README component map: 'Pull community answers with diff + conflict resolution'. Fix direction: export engine should refuse or rebase when the working tree contains un-pushed/foreign commits touching the subtree (it already clones, so rev-list origin/main..HEAD tells it); import should land updates when content genuinely differs (currently unreachable for appended-below-marker edits, see DF-23); at minimum surface per-answer detail (handler drops result.Details) so a skipped answer is distinguishable from a destroyed one.", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-28T13:47:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-28T13:47:00Z", "commit_hash": "590ada5e0ed58e18a081593ec283db51668d3ab6", "files_changed": ["internal/api/handlers.go", "internal/api/handlers_test.go", "internal/export/git.go", "internal/export/git_test.go", "pkg/api/openapi.yaml"], "guard_result": "PASS 4/4", "ci_result": "PENDING (workflow in progress)", "worker_summary": "Worker partial implementation was recovered and completed with focused export safety and import-detail regression coverage; final content commit 590ada5e; GitReins task OB-DF22-20260928 verdict beca470c PASS (Tier 1 + Tier 2).", "foreman_note": "Export now renders before checking exact target files and refuses ErrUnsafeExport before overwrite when community edits diverge from origin baseline; API returns additive non-null details and parse_errors fields. Separate conflict_strategy behavior remains DF-OFF-BY-ONE-24. Judge PASS beca470c. Content and judge commits pushed; origin/master parity verified.", "lines_added": 301, "lines_removed": 40}
 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-23", "title": "[dogfood:P1] extractSection cuts a solution body at its first embedded '---' — any corpus answer containing a horizontal rule swallows everything a community editor appends, and import then reports 'skipped: identical content' (silent no-op where an update is expected)", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "labels": ["dogfood", "export-import"], "notes": "internal/import/git.go:561-577 extractSection(content, '## Solution') returns everything up to the FIRST of \\n---\\n, \\n## , \\n# — but formatSolutionMD (internal/export/git.go:432) writes the stored solution TEXT verbatim, and corpus answers commonly END with a '---' rule inside the body (e.g. producer answer id=2 ends '...coercion (e.g., `\"toString\"` as a key).\\n\\n---'). Byte-proven 2026-09-25: appending 'Update v2' text below that rule yields a parsed solution of exactly the old 830 bytes (simulate-parse + sqlite length comparison), so importAnswer's content-diff sees no change and reports ActionSkipped 'identical content' — the community edit silently vanishes at parse time, before conflict logic could ever fire. Fix direction: cut at the LAST marker, or use a unique sentinel (e.g. a final '<!-- off-by-one:solution-end -->' comment the formatter writes), or parse into a markdown AST. Companion fix: when parsed == stored but the raw FILE bytes differ from the last exported/known bytes, report a parse_warning instead of skipped."}
 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-24", "title": "[dogfood:P2] POST /api/v1/import accepts conflict_strategy (skip|replace|manual) and returns a 'conflicted' counter — but the field is dropped at handlers.go:970 (never reaches the engine) and the engine has NO conflict/replace/manual code path at all", "priority": "P2", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "labels": ["dogfood", "export-import", "openapi"], "notes": "internal/api/handlers.go:962-970 builds importgit.Config{RepoURL, Branch, LocalDir, SubtreePrefix, GitPath} — ConflictStrategy from the request struct (handlers.go:183) is silently discarded; internal/import/git.go has exactly one Action value for conflict (ActionConflict, git.go:75) and no code that produces it, plus no replace/manual behavior. Live 2026-09-25: skip/replace/manual on identical content all return {skipped:3} identically; nothing distinguishes them. The OpenAPI spec and docs/api-reference.md 'Export / Import' section advertise this parameter. Fix direction: either implement the three strategies or reject unknown/unimplemented values with 400 'not_implemented' — a silently-ignored documented parameter is worse than its absence. Related doc gap: the import response schema has no per-answer details, so operators cannot tell WHAT was skipped; result.Details exists in the engine and is dropped by writeJSON."}
 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-25", "title": "[dogfood:P2] Empty-node bootstrap from a community repo works but is undocumented as a first-class flow — no seed, no corpus, import 3 answers, discover found:true in 156ms cold / ~90ms warm", "priority": "P2", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "labels": ["dogfood", "docs", "export-import"], "notes": "Proven 2026-09-25: a node started with a fresh -db (0 classes / 0 answers) that runs POST /api/v1/import against a community repo immediately serves discoveries for exactly the imported classes (found:true, 12-18ms) and 404s for anything else — the README's 'answers exist one step ahead of errors' loop works with zero bundled corpus, which is the lightweight community-sharing deployment most likely to matter for new adopters. docs/integration.md documents the endpoints but never this bootstrap-then-discover flow; README Core Loop step 6/7 does not mention that import is sufficient without seed. Fix direction: add a 'Join a community answers repo' subsection (3 commands: run with -import-dir, POST import, curl discover) to README + integration.md."}
